- `apps/web` auth — email-code sign-in per BP §9 (`lib/auth-server.ts`): HMAC-stored 6-digit codes, 3 requests per email per hour, 5 verify attempts then purge, atomic compare-and-delete consumption; a 15-minute HS256 access cookie (`__Host-` in production) plus a single-use refresh token (GETDEL) hashed in Redis. Request-code answers every address identically and sends after the response (CP §6.1). Find-or-create is one atomic upsert (`lib/users.ts`). Outside production, email and push reach only `OUTBOUND_ALLOWED_DOMAINS` (`lib/outbound.ts`, BP §24). The dev-login button exists only when `appEnv()` is development and `DEV_LOGIN_ENABLED=true`, decided in the `/login` server component. A refresh 401 means the session is over (sign out once); a network error or 5xx is transient (BP §9.7). Tests use `test/fake-redis.ts` and an in-memory Mongo replica set.
